ng `s` is empty or has less than three characters. If so, return `s` as is.\\n\\n2. **Grouping**:\\n   - Split the string into groups of three characters using a similar list comprehension as in `encode_cyclic`.\\n\\n3. **Decycling**:\\n   - For each group, if it has exactly three characters, cyclically shift it back by moving the last character to the beginning. Otherwise, leave it unchanged.\\n\\n4. **Joining**:\\n   - Join the modified groups back into a single string and return it.\\n\\nEdge Cases:\\n- Empty string or strings with less than three characters should be handled by returning the string unchanged.\\n- Strings with lengths not divisible by three should be correctly grouped and processed.\\n\\nComplexity:\\n- Both functions have a time complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the input string, due to the single pass required for grouping and processing."}'}]
